<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Australian and New Zealand Army Corps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1914">1914</a>–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ANZAC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Australian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> Army Corps was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> army corps formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in December 1914 under the British general William Birdwood. Its landing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> on 25 April 1915 and the costly campaign that followed made the 'Anzac' tradition a foundation of national identity in both countries. The corps was reorganised in 1916 for service on the Western Front.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/australian-and-new-zealand-army-corps.jpg" alt="Australian and New Zealand Army Corps" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GrahamBould · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anzac_Cove_encampment_1915.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
